window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>We are bound by the gods…but they didn't warn me about her.</b></p> <p>I know three important facts:</p> <p>1. My mates will do anything to keep me alive and happy.</p> <p>2. I'll do the same for them.</p> <p>3. She has a connection to my mates, and my Nexus wants her dead.</p> <p>Normal. I've never been normal for a single day of my life, but now I have to pretend to be so I can stay at the academy and train to be a ranger. Even if it costs never seeing Onyx.</p> <p>The academy is locked down for six months, and I'm not allowed to leave. No one is.</p> <p>Then she turned up. Georgina, the mystery woman who was locked up by the Vian and somehow escaped. Sweet Georgina, who has a strange connection to my rejected mates, and everyone loves…except me.</p> <p>My Nexus hates her, and every day I'm worried I'm one slip away from becoming the monster everyone fears by killing Georgina.</p> <p>I'm not normal…but neither are my mates. The more I learn about them, the more I realise I wasn't the only one born different.</p> <p>We are connected by the gods, by the very stars in the night sky, and nothing can come between us.</p> <p>Not even a Vian prince who warns me this world is about to end if I don't leave Starlight City before it's too late.</p> <p>Ethereal Shifters <i>is a dark romantasy with men who growl more than speak. You can expect tropes like Who did this to you?; touch her and die; rejected mates; forced proximity; and why-choose?</i></p>"; 
